/-- **ν and an optimal pose of `Other.HeptagonalDipyramid.polyhedron` as one root**: when the representatives' systems have
exactly one root each, of scale `N`, the system `S` has exactly one root, of scale `N`, and at it
`matAt x 45`, `matAt x 36` and `(x 54, x 55)` are a weak fit of `Other.HeptagonalDipyramid.polyhedron` scaled
by `N` through itself. -/
theorem dipyramidHeptagonalDipyramid_pose_of_reps {N : ℝ} (h : PolynomialSystem.IsRootEq [Pose.DipyramidHeptagonalDipyramid.reps0] N) :
    PolynomialSystem.IsPoseRoot Other.HeptagonalDipyramid.polyhedron Pose.DipyramidHeptagonalDipyramid.S N 45 36 54 := by
  rw [Pose.DipyramidHeptagonalDipyramid.S_eq]
  exact PolynomialSystem.ct_isPoseRoot h List.mem_cons_self Pose.DipyramidHeptagonalDipyramid.len_eq Pose.DipyramidHeptagonalDipyramid.reps_eq
    (Root.ParData.theta_spec Nieuwland.Polyhedra.DipyramidHeptagonalDipyramidDim.root) Pose.DipyramidHeptagonalDipyramid.par_ok Pose.DipyramidHeptagonalDipyramid.zs_eq Pose.DipyramidHeptagonalDipyramid.weak_ok Pose.DipyramidHeptagonalDipyramid.poly_eq Pose.DipyramidHeptagonalDipyramid.ok

end Nieuwland.Polyhedra
